book validation.average-f64
read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from ny.lang.math

require receives ok as boolean, label as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    when not ok then evaluate panic with label end when
end paragraph

!!! Oracles are nearest binary64 values of exact Fraction sums of the binary64
!!! inputs divided by count. Nonzero tolerances below are four oracle ULPs;
!!! zero tolerances deliberately cover exact results and subnormal rounding.
near receives items as array of floating, expected as floating, tolerance as floating, label as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    value result is average-f64 with arr being items
    evaluate require with ok being (result.is-some with nothing), label being label
    value actual is result.unwrap with nothing
    evaluate require with ok being (is-finite with actual), label being label
    variable lower is items at 0
    variable upper is items at 0
    repeat for index from 0 to (the length of items)
        when (items at index) is less than lower then set lower to (items at index) end when
        when (items at index) is greater than upper then set upper to (items at index) end when
    end repeat
    evaluate require with ok being (actual is at least lower and actual is at most upper), label being label
    evaluate require with ok being ((abs with (actual minus expected)) is at most tolerance), label being label
end paragraph

nan-mean receives items as array of floating, label as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    value result is average-f64 with arr being items
    evaluate require with ok being (result.is-some with nothing), label being label
    value actual is result.unwrap with nothing
    evaluate require with ok being (actual does not equal actual), label being label
end paragraph

infinite-mean receives items as array of floating, expected as floating, label as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    value result is average-f64 with arr being items
    evaluate require with ok being (result.is-some with nothing), label being label
    value actual is result.unwrap with nothing
    evaluate require with ok being (actual equals expected), label being label
end paragraph

main returns override integer begin paragraph
    value empty-mean is average-f64 with arr being []
    evaluate require with ok being (empty-mean.is-none with nothing), label being "empty mean is absent"
    evaluate near with items being [2.0, 4.0, 6.0], expected being 4.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "ordinary exact mean"
    evaluate near with items being [0.1, 0.2, 0.3], expected being 0.2, tolerance being 1.1102230246251565e-16, label being "fractional mean"
    evaluate near with items being [minus 3.0, 0.0, 3.0], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "ordinary cancellation"
    evaluate near with items being [0.0, minus 0.0], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "zero mean"
    value zero-mean is average-f64 with arr being [minus 0.0, minus 0.0]
    evaluate require with ok being ((atan2 with y being (zero-mean.unwrap with nothing), x being minus 1.0) is greater than 0.0), label being "negative-zero mean retains positive zero"
    value original is [2.0, minus 0.0, 8.0]
    value alias is original
    evaluate near with items being original, expected being 3.3333333333333335, tolerance being 1.7763568394002505e-15, label being "input alias mean"
    evaluate require with ok being ((the length of alias) equals 3 and (alias at 0) equals 2.0 and (alias at 2) equals 8.0), label being "input values preserved"
    evaluate require with ok being ((atan2 with y being (alias at 1), x being minus 1.0) is less than 0.0), label being "input negative zero preserved"
    say "ordinary means and source aliases"

    value maximum is 1.7976931348623157e308
    evaluate near with items being [maximum], expected being maximum, tolerance being 0.0, label being "maximum singleton"
    evaluate near with items being [minus maximum], expected being minus maximum, tolerance being 0.0, label being "minimum singleton"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e308], expected being 1e308, tolerance being 7.98336123813888e292, label being "positive intermediate overflow"
    evaluate near with items being [minus 1e308, minus 1e308], expected being minus 1e308, tolerance being 7.98336123813888e292, label being "negative intermediate overflow"
    evaluate near with items being [maximum, maximum, maximum], expected being maximum, tolerance being 7.98336123813888e292, label being "maximum repeated"
    evaluate near with items being [maximum, maximum, maximum, maximum, maximum], expected being maximum, tolerance being 0.0, label being "constant maximum endpoint"
    evaluate near with items being [minus maximum, minus maximum, minus maximum], expected being minus maximum, tolerance being 7.98336123813888e292, label being "minimum repeated"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e308, minus 1e308], expected being 3.333333333333333e307, tolerance being 1.99584030953472e292, label being "positive mixed overflow"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, minus 1e308, 1e308], expected being 3.333333333333333e307, tolerance being 1.99584030953472e292, label being "mixed permutation"
    evaluate near with items being [minus 1e308, minus 1e308, 1e308], expected being minus 3.333333333333333e307, tolerance being 1.99584030953472e292, label being "negative mixed overflow"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e308, minus 1e308, minus 1e308], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "balanced overflowing groups"
    evaluate near with items being [maximum, minus maximum], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "opposite maxima"
    say "finite overflow and mixed signs"

    evaluate near with items being [1e16, 1.0, minus 1e16], expected being 0.3333333333333333, tolerance being 2.220446049250313e-16, label being "moderate cancellation residue"
    evaluate near with items being [1e16, 1.0, 1.0, minus 1e16], expected being 0.5, tolerance being 0.0, label being "two cancellation units"
    evaluate near with items being [3.0, 1.0000000000000002, minus 2.0, minus 1.0, minus 1.0], expected being 4.4408920985006264e-17, tolerance being 2.465190328815662e-32, label being "compensation tail before small terms"
    evaluate near with items being [2.0000000000000004, 1.9999999999999998, minus 1.0, minus 1.0, minus 1.0, minus 1.0], expected being 3.700743415417188e-17, tolerance being 2.465190328815662e-32, label being "opposite compensation tails"
    evaluate near with items being [minus 1.0, 2.0000000000000004, minus 1.0, 1.9999999999999998, minus 1.0, minus 1.0], expected being 3.700743415417188e-17, tolerance being 2.465190328815662e-32, label being "compensation tail permutation"
    evaluate near with items being [minus 2.0000000000000004, minus 1.9999999999999998, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0], expected being minus 3.700743415417188e-17, tolerance being 2.465190328815662e-32, label being "negative compensation tails"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1.0, minus 1e308], expected being 0.3333333333333333, tolerance being 2.220446049250313e-16, label being "extreme cancellation residue"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e308, minus 1e308, minus 1e308, 3e-300], expected being 6.000000000000001e-301, tolerance being 3.3156184e-316, label being "tiny residue after overflow"
    evaluate near with items being [3e-300, minus 1e308, 1e308, minus 1e308, 1e308], expected being 6.000000000000001e-301, tolerance being 3.3156184e-316, label being "tiny residue permutation"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e-308, minus 1e308], expected being 3.33333333333333e-309, tolerance being 2e-323, label being "subnormal cancellation residue"
    evaluate near with items being [maximum, minus maximum, 2.2250738585072014e-308], expected being 7.41691286169067e-309, tolerance being 2e-323, label being "minimum normal residue"
    evaluate near with items being [1e308, 1e308, minus 1e308, minus 1e308, 5e-324], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "unrepresentable final residue rounds to zero"
    say "compensated cancellation"

    value tiny is 5e-324
    evaluate near with items being [tiny, tiny], expected being tiny, tolerance being 0.0, label being "repeated minimum subnormal"
    evaluate near with items being [minus tiny, minus tiny], expected being minus tiny, tolerance being 0.0, label being "negative minimum subnormal"
    evaluate near with items being [tiny, 0.0, tiny], expected being tiny, tolerance being 0.0, label being "subnormal thirds"
    evaluate near with items being [tiny, 0.0], expected being 0.0, tolerance being 0.0, label being "subnormal tie rounds to even zero"
    evaluate near with items being [1.5e-323, 0.0], expected being 1e-323, tolerance being 0.0, label being "subnormal tie rounds to even nonzero"
    evaluate near with items being [tiny, 1e-323, 1.5e-323], expected being 1e-323, tolerance being 0.0, label being "mixed subnormal mean"
    evaluate near with items being [2.2250738585072014e-308, 2.2250738585072014e-308, 2.2250738585072014e-308], expected being 2.2250738585072014e-308, tolerance being 0.0, label being "minimum normal repeated"
    evaluate near with items being [2.2250738585072014e-308, 2.225073858507201e-308], expected being 2.2250738585072014e-308, tolerance being 0.0, label being "normal boundary tie"
    say "subnormal means and rounding"

    variable large-values as array of floating is []
    variable small-values as array of floating is []
    repeat for index from 0 to 257
        append maximum to large-values
        append tiny to small-values
    end repeat
    evaluate near with items being large-values, expected being maximum, tolerance being 7.98336123813888e292, label being "257 maximum values"
    evaluate near with items being small-values, expected being tiny, tolerance being 0.0, label being "257 minimum subnormals"
    say "repeated maximum and subnormal means"

    value infinity is exp with 1000.0
    value nan is sqrt with minus 1.0
    evaluate infinite-mean with items being [infinity], expected being infinity, label being "positive infinity singleton"
    evaluate infinite-mean with items being [minus infinity], expected being minus infinity, label being "negative infinity singleton"
    evaluate infinite-mean with items being [infinity, 1e308, 1e308], expected being infinity, label being "positive infinity propagates"
    evaluate infinite-mean with items being [minus infinity, 1e308, 1e308], expected being minus infinity, label being "negative infinity precedes large terms"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [nan], label being "NaN singleton"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [1.0, nan, 2.0], label being "NaN inside input"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [infinity, minus infinity], label being "opposite infinities"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [infinity, nan, minus infinity], label being "NaN and infinities"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [1e308, 1e308, minus infinity], label being "historical overflow before opposite infinity"
    evaluate nan-mean with items being [minus 1e308, minus 1e308, infinity], label being "historical negative overflow before infinity"
    evaluate require with ok being ((sum-f64 with arr being [1e308, 1e308]) equals infinity), label being "sum retains ordinary overflowing arithmetic"
    say "nonfinite input contracts"
    give 0
end paragraph
